   "body": "### Capture result (mac/capture-batch, run 9, PR #400)\nCorpus id: `R96a` (user1's MP list, `page=8` of 7, with `MPStorage.m:694`'s query; legacy oracle `LOT-002/R96a.oracle.json`). Also `R95j` (an empty list after a thread delete).\n- The page past the last page is **not** a `.hop` page: 200, no redirect, the list header and no topic row, `<title>` \"… - Page : 8\", the pager lists 1 to 7 as links (no current page), \"Page Précédente\" links page 7, no \"Page Suivante\".\n- So a `.notAuthenticated` (a `.hop`) on any MP list page is a login wall, not \"past the end\".\n\nChanges: follow-up #402 (parser test on `R96a`, drop the \"never captured\" caveat of `PrivateMessageListParser`). Fact in HFR-PROTOCOL §6b \"MP list past the last page\".\n",
   "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
